    "created_at": "2017-10-04T10:09:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-04T10:09:54Z",
    "body": "As a start, I think it would help if we moved underflow/overflow checks to the value sanitization algorithm rather than have them apply all the time.\r\n\r\nThe other thing that seems to be needed here however is that whenever `max` or `min` is set, the value is sanitized as well. That's needed because they influence the initial value. Without that happening the initial value would always be dependent on when `min` and `max` are set, as far as I can tell.\r\n\r\n@jessi3py would you agree with that analysis? (For context, we basically don't want the order in which you set attributes to end up mattering.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
