    "created_at": "2017-10-09T04:32:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-10-09T04:32:50Z",
    "body": "In Firefox's implementation, we do sanitize the value when min/max is set. But in our sanitization algorithm, we set it to the middle value only if there is no value set (including content attribute and initial value), otherwise we clamp the value based on min/max.\r\n\r\nSo I think the question is still whether we should force set it to the middle value when value has not changed by the user?\r\n\r\nLet me know if I'm missing anything.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
